HST Office: compact banner for windows narrower than 1280 px, and an exact artwork ratio for the slot.

Owner decision (2026-11-07): the banner always keeps its slot; narrow windows show a compact banner.

- sfx2/source/notebookbar/HstBannerGeometry.hxx: modeFor() picks Wide (windows of at least 1280
  logical px), Compact (narrower) or Hidden (one-row ribbons); artWidth() is 360 or 160 logical px.
  slotFor() now keeps the exact artwork ratio (360:104 or 160:104) and centres the slot vertically
  on the page, so a taller page no longer gives a 360x125 slot around 360x104 art.
- sfx2/source/notebookbar/HstRibbonBanner.{hxx,cxx}: SetCompact() switches between the wide and
  the 160x104 compact artwork and starts the rotation again for the new ratio. The compact slot
  asks org.hst.office.BannerFeed with Compact=true (older data layers are asked as before) and
  reads imageCompact from the installed defaults; it rotates through items with compact art only,
  the wide art is never cropped. When neither has compact art the slot is hidden and the groups
  get the width; that is asked again after 10 minutes. Click targets: HTTPS, or the local test
  server, which the data layer only accepts in test-stamped packages.
- sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx, sfx2/inc/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.hxx:
  the layout uses the mode and the compact slot, and lays out again when the banner reports that no
  compact art exists.
Unit test: tests/unit/test_ribbon_banner_compact.py.

